{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game","id":532133,"title":"The \"Would You If\" Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-29T12:49:49-07:00","id":532133,"title":"The \"Would You If\" Game","content":"I miss when we played forum games, so I'm going to start a new one.<br /> <br /> I'm going to post a hypothetical with a big benefit but a significant drawback. You may answer or you may post a scenario of your own following the same template. I won't answer the one I'm about to post because I mean to use this as a jumping-off point for a great big post when I get home, but future posters are welcome to answer their own.<br /> <br /> <b>My hypothetical scenario is:</b><br /> <br /> You are offered the opportunity to relive your life with the benefit of all the knowledge and experience you currently possess, so you could undo the wrongs and the harms you have done to yourself and others, or just convince your parents to invest in Microsoft so you'll be rich; whatever floats your boat. However, the way the procedure works, your consciousness has to be implanted in your past self at the moment your umbilical cord is cut, so you will spend years as a baby, unable to communicate or control your motor functions, and there's no guarantee that by the time you're able to act on your memories, you will still remember them. Hell, there's no guarantee the isolation inside your brain won't drive you crazy.<br /> <br /> Would you take the chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:25:54-07:00","id":532177,"title":"","content":"No. What's done is done. Remember the past, but live in the present, and look to the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:27:59-07:00","id":532181,"title":"","content":"Hell, yes, but my grandfather had stock in Apple at one time and (foolishly) sold it. I'd just have him keep that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The madness of being inside one's own brain is nothing new to me, so remove 99% of the stressors I have in my life, and I think I can handle it.<br /> <br /> Soon as I can write, I'll start making a journal just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T13:30:29-07:00","id":532186,"title":"","content":"No, dear god, no. The drawbacks are too painful, my teenage years were awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T15:00:28-07:00","id":534877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game#post532133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss when we played forum games, so I'm going to start a new one.<br /> <br /> I'm going to post a hypothetical with a big benefit but a significant drawback. You may answer or you may post a scenario of your own following the same template. I won't answer the one I'm about to post because I mean to use this as a jumping-off point for a great big post when I get home, but future posters are welcome to answer their own.<br /> <br /> <b>My hypothetical scenario is:</b><br /> <br /> You are offered the opportunity to relive your life with the benefit of all the knowledge and experience you currently possess, so you could undo the wrongs and the harms you have done to yourself and others, or just convince your parents to invest in Microsoft so you'll be rich; whatever floats your boat. However, the way the procedure works, your consciousness has to be implanted in your past self at the moment your umbilical cord is cut, so you will spend years as a baby, unable to communicate or control your motor functions, and there's no guarantee that by the time you're able to act on your memories, you will still remember them. Hell, there's no guarantee the isolation inside your brain won't drive you crazy.<br /> <br /> Would you take the chance?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but I'd be the crazed King of an apocalyptic hellscape right now. <br /> <br /> Good thing this is hypothetical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T17:56:57-07:00","id":534984,"title":"","content":"I place odds on me making it, ear infection and everything. So growing up with the wisdom I have with the chance to change some crucial moments? Hell yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T03:40:31-07:00","id":535407,"title":"","content":"No. I'd just trade one set of idiotic mistakes for another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T05:43:48-07:00","id":535479,"title":"","content":"Fuck yes. Youth is wasted on the young, as they say; I'd be all over getting to be young with the knowledge and maturity of a grown-up. Given the memory of my hopefully long previous life, the baby years probably won't even seen that long by comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:07:47-07:00","id":537666,"title":"","content":"Right now I likely would not, at least not unless I'm capable of getting more information on how all those memories would interact with my undeveloped newborn brain. Ask me 30 years from now and there will likely be a higher chance that I'll jump on the opportunity even if I don't have much info. As the age goes up from there the likelihood of me accepting probably increases, or if at some point while still lucid I get to know I have initial signs of dementia or Alzheimer's or something like that, at that point I'd very probably take the chance.<br /> <br /> <b>Here is another hypothetical</b>: If you could greatly increase a human capacity or greatly decrease a human limitation, while still keeping at least semi-plausible to the laws of reality if you don't analyze it too hard, what would it be? You can assume changes to the body or mind necessary for your thing to happen are part of the package, as long as the final result is still recognizably human for the most part. Keep in mind not only you would change, but all of humanity from this point onward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 06-02-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T20:14:16-07:00","id":537674,"title":"","content":"I'd do it. The living your life over again thing. I've had some pretty significant life changes that could have been avoided or taken advantage of if I knew more beforehand. Enough that it would be worth it, and considering my state in high school I'd probably have met my wife if I went insane anyways and I certainly would of had I forgotten, since I'd probably just be doing it all over the same way.<br /> <br /> @danelsan Can you give an example? Also, are you talking about for all of humanity or simply the respondent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T05:52:01-07:00","id":538121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game?p=537674#post537674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@danelsan Can you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Personally, I would vastly increase human capacity for empathy/compassion, hopefully to the point anyone can include most of humanity in their &quot;monkey sphere&quot;.<br /> Another example could be drastically reducing human need for nourishment, or giving our already impressive stamina a huge boost, or making it so we can grow incredibly tall, or making our brains capable of processing information much faster and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, are you talking about for all of humanity or simply the respondent? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game?p=537666#post537666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind not only you would change, but all of humanity from this point onward.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T11:13:11-07:00","id":538571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game#post532133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are offered the opportunity to relive your life with the benefit of all the knowledge and experience you currently possess, so you could undo the wrongs and the harms you have done to yourself and others, or just convince your parents to invest in Microsoft so you'll be rich; whatever floats your boat. However, the way the procedure works, your consciousness has to be implanted in your past self at the moment your umbilical cord is cut, so you will spend years as a baby, unable to communicate or control your motor functions, and there's no guarantee that by the time you're able to act on your memories, you will still remember them. Hell, there's no guarantee the isolation inside your brain won't drive you crazy.<br /> <br /> Would you take the chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would. I can't do it for the sake of fixing myself, because I will by the nature of the process still be saddled with memories of the failures I've committed, but I could do things better for the people in my life who matter. I'd have to be very, very sure I kept the chain of events that got me the friends I've made, though. Of everything in my life, that is the most important to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game?p=537666#post537666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could greatly increase a human capacity or greatly decrease a human limitation, while still keeping at least semi-plausible to the laws of reality if you don't analyze it too hard, what would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say I'd reduce our vulnerability to dementia. People deserve to die better deaths than the ones Alzheimer's inflict.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T04:13:16-07:00","id":539421,"title":"","content":"To JimB's hypothetical:<br /> Yes. Yes, I most assuredly would.<br /> I would jump at the chance to change things and perfect my actions. Sure I may make mistakes the second time around, but I did the first time too.<br /> <br /> To Danelsan's hypothetical:<br /> I would make mankind wiser to our follies. Maybe then we wouldn't make so many stupid and pointless mistakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-04T07:52:02-07:00","id":539525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game?p=537666#post537666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Here is another hypothetical</b>: If you could greatly increase a human capacity or greatly decrease a human limitation, while still keeping at least semi-plausible to the laws of reality if you don't analyze it too hard, what would it be? You can assume changes to the body or mind necessary for your thing to happen are part of the package, as long as the final result is still recognizably human for the most part. Keep in mind not only you would change, but all of humanity from this point onward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, gonna be blunt and trollish with this one, but ghods save me from the stupid people. Whatever I would need to do to make people more aware, open-minded, tolerant and <u><i><b>actually able to keep to the ideals we so often claim are so important to us</b></i></u>..........whatever part of us it is that would need to increase or decrease, that is what I would change. And yes, myself included. At least I <i>know </i>I'm an asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T22:56:20-07:00","id":544841,"title":"","content":"Hehe, I wonder how old is everybody who is giving JimB an enthusiastic yes on his hypothetical, because I feel some people might be just kinda skipping that Jim made it pretty risky, and you may end up just throwing away all the time you would still have in your life (&quot;knowledge and experience you <i>currently</i> possess&quot;) and/or completely fucking up the part you are re-living and the part you haven't lived yet (by going insane, for instance).<br /> <br /> Some more hypotheticals, if anyone wants to answer one or more of them:<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b> If you could trade one of your hands (with the remaining stump healing well and instantaneously, no pain at all) for any one object in the world, would you do it? And if so, what object would that be?<br /> <br /> <b>2)</b> If you could selectively* get any and all the knowledge, experiences, skills and expertise of any one person in history added to your own (as if you had gone through the studying, practice and experiences they did), who would you &quot;absorb&quot;?<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">By which I mean you don't have to get everything. Like, if you want the mathematical skills of some famous scientist but don't want their views on religion interfering with your own, you can get just the math wizardry</span>.<br /> <br /> <b>3)</b> You get to imprint your moral sensibilities and ideals into a currently living figure of authority and/or influence, to the point they now firmly in the same broad &quot;camp&quot; as you on every major issue, and to a somewhat lesser degree the same goes for their closer allies, advisers, confidantes, family and so on. Who would you choose?<br /> <br /> <b>4)</b> If you could bring back to life any one fully-human person from history (so, if you believe someone had divine qualities, or was part alien or something like that, they are disqualified from resurrection), and this person would instantly be blessed with basic knowledge of modern society enough to have no more cultural shock than any one of us visiting a different country, who would you bring back, if anyone?<br /> <br /> <b>5)</b> If you could magically get, with perfect recall, a detailed answer to a single question that science currently can't answer completely or definitely, what question would you get an answer for?<br /> <br /> There is a soft limit on the scope of the questions, though: questions like &quot;is there an afterlife?&quot;, &quot;how do blackholes work?&quot;, or &quot;Are there other civilizations outside of Earth?&quot; are OK.<br /> Hugely broad stuff like &quot;what is the truth?&quot;, &quot;how does the universe works?&quot; or &quot;what is all of history like?&quot; is not permitted.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that the answer will be in terms of actual reality: if you ask &quot;how can I generate infinite energy?&quot; and it turns out it really is impossible to do so, you will know in detail why it is impossible, not learn how to do it despite it being impossible - you get information, not magic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T06:51:10-07:00","id":545129,"title":"","content":"1. I wouldn't, for a single object. Maybe if there was a viable trillion dollar bill. Maybe a particularly valuable bond of some sort, but I'd have to do research.<br /> 2. Jesus would be tempting, just to see what really was going on. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OclYAJhyNY0\" target=\"_blank\">But apparently he was a lousy carpenter.</a> Siddhartha might be a nice alternative. But someone like Harold Williams might be more practical, as enlightenment won't feed my family.<br /> 3. Absolutely no one.<br /> 4. My mother.<br /> 5. How can I obtain the closest alternatives to eternal life? Gotta love wordplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-08-2015, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T08:48:00-07:00","id":545355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game?p=544841#post544841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1)</b> If you could trade one of your hands (with the remaining stump healing well and instantaneously, no pain at all) for any one object in the world, would you do it? And if so, what object would that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuclear Warhead. It would sit in my parents backyard, every now and again I'd post images of children playing on it, on the internet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>2)</b> If you could selectively* get any and all the knowledge, experiences, skills and expertise of any one person in history added to your own (as if you had gone through the studying, practice and experiences they did), who would you &quot;absorb&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Temujin. I don't even care if what I learn will be utterly worthless to me. I have google.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You get to imprint your moral sensibilities and ideals into a currently living figure of authority and/or influence, to the point they now firmly in the same broad &quot;camp&quot; as you on every major issue, and to a somewhat lesser degree the same goes for their closer allies, advisers, confidantes, family and so on. Who would you choose? </div> </div> </div>Sean Hannity. Because by god, that would cause an amusing shitstorm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>4)</b> If you could bring back to life any one fully-human person from history (so, if you believe someone had divine qualities, or was part alien or something like that, they are disqualified from resurrection), and this person would instantly be blessed with basic knowledge of modern society enough to have no more cultural shock than any one of us visiting a different country, who would you bring back, if anyone? </div> </div> </div>One of my Grandads. Not sure if it should be on my mom or dad's side though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>5)</b> If you could magically get, with perfect recall, a detailed answer to a single question that science currently can't answer completely or definitely, what question would you get an answer for? </div> </div> </div>&quot;What should I do now?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T23:43:43-07:00","id":686612,"title":"","content":"*hope no one hates me for bumping an old thread but i''m bored*<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b><b> If you could trade one of your hands (with the remaining stump healing well and instantaneously, no pain at all) for any one object in the world, would you do it? And if so, what object would that be?</b><br /> The worlds largest diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I need money!<br /> <br /> <b>2)</b><b> If you could selectively* get any and all the knowledge, experiences, skills and expertise of any one person in history added to your own (as if you had gone through the studying, practice and experiences they did), who would you &quot;absorb&quot;?</b><br /> i'll come back to this one!<br /> <br /> <b>3</b><b>)</b> <b>You get to imprint your moral sensibilities and ideals into a currently living figure of authority and/or influence, to the point they now firmly in the same broad &quot;camp&quot; as you on every major issue, and to a somewhat lesser degree the same goes for their closer allies, advisers, confidantes, family and so on. Who would you choose?</b><br /> <br /> My fiance XDD he counts right? he IS technically an authority figure to our daughter lol We dont see anything the same way!<br /> <br /> <b>4)</b><b> If you could bring back to life any one fully-human person from history (so, if you believe someone had divine qualities, or was part alien or something like that, they are disqualified from resurrection), and this person would instantly be blessed with basic knowledge of modern society enough to have no more cultural shock than any one of us visiting a different country, who would you bring back, if anyone?</b><br /> <br /> I' going to explain first cause uh it will be totally fucking wrong of me if i dont.Growing up i was fascinated by the holocaust, not because of what was done but because i wanted to understand HOW people could do that, and why. It saddend me deeply that such a thing happened. I want to pick the brain of Hitler, i want to have an indepth no holds barred conversation with that horrible man to understand more of his motivations, why it was done and how involved he was with the events that took place. Likely when i was done i'd put a bullet in his head...because a man like that doesnt deserve a seond chance at life.<br /> <br /> <b>5)</b> <b>If you could magically get, with perfect recall, a detailed answer to a single question that science currently can't answer completely or definitely, what question would you get an answer for?</b><br /> <br /> I know this is going to be SUPER typical but i'd want to know if the gods exsist. does this count? If not,i'd want to know if seeing the future is real or not.<br /> <br /> i'm gonna throw one out there:<br /> <br /> <b><i><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">You are offered the opportunity of your lifetime, you can have the ONE thing you want most in your life(perfect health, magic powers(only one dont be that guy...so if you want mind reading its yours, flight etc), infinite cash things like that no holds barred), BUT you must give up the thing you currently consider the most important thing to you. (be it your spouse, child, health etc. It MUST be something truely important something your normally wouldnt even consider giving up no matter what the price.)</span></i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","user":"Scelesta","date":". 10-03-2015, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T12:34:58-07:00","id":690146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/532133-the-would-you-if-game